    questionText: "Describe any three of the following: (i) Iron ore, (ii) Galvanised steel, (iii) Tuyere, (iv) Tinplate.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 9,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "Iron Ore: Iron ore is the rock that iron comes from. Iron ore is smelted in the blast furnace to produce pig iron, which in turn is refined to produce steel.", marks: 9, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":3,"options":["Iron Ore: Iron ore is the rock that iron comes from. Iron ore is smelted in the blast furnace to produce pig iron, which in turn is refined to produce steel.","Galvanised steel: Steel in its raw state rusts when exposed to moisture. Galvanised steel is steel coated with zinc to prevent the oxygen attacking the surface of the steel and causing it to rust.","Tuyere: A tuyere is an air pipe which surrounds the blast furnace. The tuyere allows hot blasts of air to be delivered inside the blast furnace thereby increasing the temperature of the process through the burning of coke.","Tinplate: Tinplate is thin sheets of steel coated in tin. The tin protects the steel from rusting as well as giving it an attractive appearance. Tinplate is widely used for food containers as it is non-toxic and easily soldered."]} },
    ],
